Speech models (downloaded separately, never inside the installer; see docs/MODELS.md):

- Parakeet TDT 0.6B v3 by NVIDIA, licensed under CC BY 4.0
  (https://huggingface.co/nvidia/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3). Used as converted to ONNX and quantised to int8
  by the sherpa-onnx project (https://huggingface.co/csukuangfj/sherpa-onnx-nemo-parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3-int8).
- WeSpeaker ResNet34-LM speaker embedding (wenet-e2e/wespeaker), trained on VoxCeleb, licensed under CC BY 4.0,
  as converted to ONNX by sherpa-onnx. Changed on the user's computer by Prism Transcribe's installer: one
  metadata entry appended (feature_normalize_type = global-mean) so the runtime removes each utterance's mean.
- Silero VAD, Copyright (c) 2020-present Silero Team, MIT licence.
- Heavy pack (optional): Whisper large-v3-turbo by OpenAI, MIT licence, in whisper.cpp's format
  (https://huggingface.co/ggerganov/whisper.cpp).

Separate programs run by Prism Transcribe (not linked into it):

- whisper.cpp's whisper-cli (MIT licence, https://github.com/ggml-org/whisper.cpp), for the heavy pack.

Code built into the program:

- sherpa-onnx (Apache License 2.0) and ONNX Runtime (MIT), linked statically. vendor/sherpa-onnx carries one
  small change, described in vendor/PATCHES.md.
- The RustCrypto project's argon2 and chacha20poly1305 crates (MIT or Apache License 2.0), for password protection.

Used from Windows itself (not shipped): the Windows spell checker (ISpellChecker), for the de-identification
suggestions pass.
